  "body": "Found 2026-11-09 while reviewing the GPU fixes (#604, #613). Every GPU test requests wgpu's **software** adapter:\n- `crates/ui/tests/gpu_render.rs:30`, `trace_composite.rs:30`, `trace_parity.rs:25`;\n- the headless shell run, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs:1565` (`headless_run_succeeds`, and through it the two `*_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero` tests).\n\nAll of them pass `RequestAdapterOptions { force_fallback_adapter: true, .. }`.\n\n**What that does on each platform:**\n- **Linux and Windows:** there is a software adapter (lavapipe, WARP), so these tests render.\n- **macOS:** Metal has **no software fallback**, so the request always fails (\"metal had no fallback adapters\"), on every Mac, with a real GPU present.\n\n**Effect on macOS:**\n- `gpu_render`, `trace_composite` and `trace_parity` return early from `device_and_queue() -> None` and **pass without rendering**. They are silent skips, so a shader regression can't fail them on a Mac.\n- `headless_run_succeeds` and the two headless CLI tests **fail** with \"No suitable graphics adapter found\". This has been read as \"this Mac has no GPU\", which is wrong.\n\n**Expected:**\n- **Adapter choice:** request the software adapter first (deterministic on CI), and on failure request the platform's default hardware adapter (`force_fallback_adapter: false`, low power). The tests then render on a Mac's real Metal GPU.\n- **No silent skips:** a test with no adapter at all prints that it skipped, so a skip is never read as a pass. A deliberate \"skip when no adapter\" stays possible for headless CI without a GPU.\n\n**Done means:**\n- on macOS, `gpu_render` / `trace_composite` / `trace_parity` actually render (each asserts it drew pixels) and `headless_run_succeeds` passes;\n- a test that found no adapter says so in its output;\n- Linux and Windows still pick the software adapter.\n\nRelated: #604 (its `gpu_render` result on macOS was a skip), #613, #605.\n",
